# Dev Containers Quick Start

The default location for usage snippets is the `samples` directory.

## Running a Usage Sample

A sample usage example has been provided in a `root.{{.Local.FileSuffix}}` file. As you work with the SDK, it's expected that you will modify these samples to fit your needs. To execute this particular snippet, use the command below.

```
{{.Local.FileExecution}} root.{{.Local.FileSuffix}}
```

## Generating Additional Usage Samples

The speakeasy CLI allows you to generate more usage snippets. Here's how:

- To generate a sample for a specific operation by providing an operation ID, use:

```
speakeasy generate usage -s {{.Local.SchemaPath}} -l {{.Local.Language}} -i {INPUT_OPERATION_ID} -o ./samples
```

- To generate samples for an entire namespace (like a tag or group name), use:

```
speakeasy generate usage -s {{.Local.SchemaPath}} -l {{.Local.Language}} -n {INPUT_TAG_NAME} -o ./samples
```
